10. Advantages
Easy to understand and implement.
Demonstrates fundamental cryptographic principles.
Suitable for beginners learning cybersecurity.
Requires minimal computational resources.
11. Limitations
Vulnerable to brute-force attacks.
Not suitable for real-world secure communications.
Uses a fixed substitution pattern.
Easily broken using frequency analysis.
12. Conclusion

The Caesar Cipher Encryption and Decryption project successfully demonstrates the fundamental concepts of cryptography. The implementation shows how information can be transformed into ciphertext and restored to its original form using a shift key. While the Caesar Cipher is not secure for modern applications, it provides a strong foundation for understanding encryption, decryption, and data protection mechanisms used in cybersecurity.

